<title>UK: Germans seek free market grains at EU tender.</title>
<headline>Germans seek free market grains at EU tender.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders bid for 19,800 tonnes of wheat and 3,000 tonnes of barley at Thursday's EU open market grain export tender, the state grain intervention board BLE said by telephone from Frankfurt.</p>
<p>Bids were for refunds ranging from 5.35 to 10.35 Ecus for the wheat and 29.97-31.25 Ecus for the barley.</p>
<p>The tender will be adjudicated on Thursday afternoon by the EU cereals management committee.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
